{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false},"description":"Creates, updates, deletes, links or unlinks records. updateMany applies one shared patch atomically to a typed target array; deleteMany previews and deletes the whole selection atomically. Each target carries its latest version. Writes use field-assignment arrays and stable references. Omitted fields remain unchanged; null explicitly clears an optional input. A full Formatted text replacement writes {kind: 'richText', documentJson: '<ProseMirror document JSON string>'}; Markdown is returned on read but is not accepted for full replacement. A file value lists the ids of uploaded files in order and replaces the files in the field, so the ids to keep are included; an address value sends its parts and is stored unverified unless it is {kind: 'address', candidateToken} from an address lookup. To add Markdown to a Formatted text or single Text field without rewriting it, an update sends { fieldId, append }: the text is added after the current value with a blank line, and an update that only appends cannot conflict with a newer record version. Phone numbers, email addresses and social profiles are the record's identities, sent as mutation.identities (provider and value) on create or update, with fields: [] when nothing else changes; the list replaces the contact details, so the existing ones to keep are included. Calculated fields cannot be written. An idempotency key identifies one exact payload, and a retry of that payload reuses it. A version conflict is rejected with the current version of each target, which is the expectedVersion for a retry. delete and deleteMany move the records, their sub-list rows and cascading records to Trash, where they stay restorable for 30 days; the result carries trashBatchId identifying the whole delete. permanent: true deletes permanently right away (erasure requests) and cannot be undone. The impactHash of a deletion preview, passed as expectedImpactHash, rejects the deletion when its cascading effects changed. Pending operations pause workspace CRM writes and preserve the previous complete state for reads.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"expectedRevision":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"idempotencyKey":{"maxLength":200,"minLength":8,"type":"string"},"mutation":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"create requires typeId and fields; update requires ref, expectedVersion and fields, where a field entry is { fieldId, value } or, for Formatted text and Text fields, { fieldId, append } to add text after the current value (an update that only appends cannot conflict with a newer version); an update may carry placement to move the record in the list's manual order; delete requires ref and expectedVersion and moves the record (with its sub-list rows and cascaded records) to Trash, where it stays restorable for 30 days; permanent: true deletes it permanently right away and erases its values from history. link/unlink require relationId, source and target. updateMany/deleteMany require targets with each ref and expectedVersion; updateMany requires fields and applies the same patch to every target atomically; deleteMany moves every target to Trash (permanent: true deletes them permanently). Only the fields of that action are allowed. Phone numbers, email addresses and social profiles are not fields: create and update carry them as identities inside this mutation object (with fields: [] when nothing else changes), and the list replaces the record's contact details, so it includes the ones to keep.","properties":{"action":{"enum":["create","update","delete","link","unlink","updateMany","deleteMany"],"type":"string"},"assignedUserIds":{"items":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"},"maxItems":100,"type":"array"},"captureFieldIds":{"items":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"},"maxItems":100,"type":"array"},"expectedImpactHash":{"description":"Optional. When given, it must equal the impactHash of a current deletion preview (POST /v1/records/preview-deletion); the delete fails with a conflict if the impact changed since.","pattern":"^[a-f0-9]{64}$","type":"string"},"expectedVersion":{"exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":9007199254740991,"type":"integer"},"fields":{"items":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"fieldId":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"},"value":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Typed CRM value; only the fields for the selected kind are allowed. A decimal carries a currency, null when it has none. For richText writes send documentJson as a ProseMirror document JSON string, not the Markdown returned on read. A file value lists uploaded file ids in order; the server formats an address value from its parts.","properties":{"candidateToken":{"description":"Address only, in place of value: a candidateToken from an address lookup stores the verified address.","maxLength":4096,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"currency":{"anyOf":[{"pattern":"^[A-Z]{3}$","type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"documentJson":{"maxLength":1000000,"pattern":"^[^\\u0000]*$","type":"string"},"end":{"anyOf":[{"pattern":"^[^\\u0000]*$","type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"kind":{"enum":["text","textList","decimal","boolean","date","dateTime","range","select","selectList","member","richText","file","address"],"type":"string"},"start":{"anyOf":[{"pattern":"^[^\\u0000]*$","type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"value":{"anyOf":[{"maxLength":100000,"pattern":"^[^\\u0000]*$","type":"string"},{"type":"boolean"},{"items":{"maxLength":100000,"pattern":"^[^\\u0000]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":100,"minItems":1,"type":"array"},{"additionalProperties":{},"properties":{"city":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"countryCode":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"line2":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"postalCode":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"region":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"street":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]}},"type":"object"}]}},"required":["kind"],"type":"object"},{"type":"null"}]}},"required":["fieldId","value"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"append":{"description":"Markdown for a Formatted text field or plain text for a Text field, added after the current value with a blank line in between.","maxLength":65535,"type":"string"},"fieldId":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"}},"required":["fieldId","append"],"type":"object"}]},"maxItems":250,"type":"array"},"identities":{"description":"Replaces this record's contact details (phone numbers, email addresses and social profiles) on a list with a channels field. Omit to preserve; [] unlinks this record. Existing shared identities remain unchanged.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"displayName":{"anyOf":[{"maxLength":500,"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"messagingId":{"anyOf":[{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"profileUrl":{"anyOf":[{"format":"uri","maxLength":2000,"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"provider":{"description":"mail is an email address, stored in lowercase; google and outlook mark an address synced from Gmail or Outlook, and one address is one identity whichever provider is given. phone is a plain phone number in international format with + or 00 and its country dialling code; it is stored in E.164 and matches WhatsApp chats from the same number. whatsapp marks a number synced from WhatsApp. One number is one identity whichever of the two is given.","enum":["google","outlook","mail","linkedin","whatsapp","instagram","telegram","facebook","phone"],"type":"string"},"value":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["provider","value"],"type":"object"},"maxItems":100,"type":"array"},"linkChanges":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"action":{"enum":["link","unlink"],"type":"string"},"direction":{"enum":["outgoing","incoming"],"type":"string"},"record":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"recordId":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"},"typeId":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"}},"required":["typeId","recordId"],"type":"object"},"relationId":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"}},"required":["action","relationId","direction","record"],"type":"object"},"maxItems":100,"type":"array"},"links":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"direction":{"enum":["outgoing","incoming"],"type":"string"},"record":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"recordId":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"},"typeId":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"}},"required":["typeId","recordId"],"type":"object"},"relationId":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"}},"required":["relationId","direction","record"],"type":"object"},"maxItems":100,"type":"array"},"permanent":{"type":"boolean"},"placement":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Moves the record in its list's manual order (sort system:manual): right after afterRecordId, right before beforeRecordId, between both, or first when neither is given. With groupFieldId (a single choice input field, not a calculated one), the order is kept within records that share the record's value of that field, as in a board column. Changing only the order creates no new version, history entry or webhook.","properties":{"afterRecordId":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"},"beforeRecordId":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"},"groupFieldId":{"format":"uuid","pattern":"^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"ref":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"recordId":{"f